  "prompt": "=== Chain-of-thought analysis prompt ===\nYou are a software requirements analyst preparing a UML state machine model.\n\nAnalyze the requirement and extract only the modeling facts needed for a state transition diagram. Keep the analysis concise and evidence-based.\n\nReturn the analysis using exactly these headings:\nStates:\nInitial state:\nFinal states:\nEvents or conditions:\nTransitions:\nMissing or ambiguous details:\n\nDo not write PlantUML in this step.\n\nRequirement:\nWeather Station System — Polished Requirement Specification\n\nFunctional Requirements\n1. The system shall restart and begin running from a shut down condition.\n2. The system shall enter configuration mode when changes or power-saving settings are required.\n3. The system shall return to running state after configuration is completed.\n4. The system shall collect data when triggered by the clock while running.\n5. The system shall prepare and send out a weather summary upon request.\n6. The system shall check its own status and transmit the result upon request.\n7. The system shall return to running state after performing an activity (data collection, summary preparation, or status checking).\n8. The system shall move into a controlled mode through remote control.\n9. The system shall return to shut down condition if a shutdown command is given while running.\n\n=== Chain-of-thought analysis response ===\nStates:\n- Shut Down\n- Running\n- Configuration Mode\n- Controlled Mode\n\nInitial state:\nShut Down\n\nFinal states:\nRunning, Configuration Mode, Controlled Mode (not explicitly stated as final, but these are the end states)\n\nEvents or conditions:\n- Restart Command\n- Changes or Power-Saving Settings Required\n- Clock Trigger\n- Request for Weather Summary\n- Request for Status Check\n- Remote Control Command\n- Shutdown Command\n\nTransitions:\n1. Shut Down -> Running: Upon receiving a Restart Command.\n2. Running -> Configuration Mode: When Changes or Power-Saving Set